+---
+type: spec
+task_slug: reject-zero-duration
+status: approved
+created: 2026-10-15
+tags: [timeparse, spec, python, validation, duration]
+test_framework: pytest
+interview_rounds: 1
+lane: light
+summary: "parse_duration rejects a zero total; all other package functions unchanged"
+---
+
+# SPEC: reject-zero-duration
+
+## 🎯 Intent
+A zero duration used as a timeout is always a mistake (it means "expire immediately" or "never", depending on the consumer). `parse_duration` should refuse it so the mistake surfaces at parse time.
+
+## 🌅 Outcomes
+- `parse_duration` raises `ValueError` for any input whose total is zero.
+- Every other function in the package (`normalize`, `total`, `format_duration`, the CLI) behaves exactly as before, including accepting zero.
+
+## 📋 In-Scope Scenarios
+
+### S1: zero total is rejected
+**Given** the strings `"0s"`, `"0h0m"`, `" 0D "`, `"00s"`, `"0d0h0m0s"` and `"0m0s"`
+**When** each is passed to `parse_duration`
+**Then** each raises `ValueError`
+
+### S2: zero unit in a non-zero duration is accepted
+**Given** the strings `"0h1m"` and `"1h0m"`
+**When** each is passed to `parse_duration`
+**Then** they return 60 and 3600 respectively
+
+### S3: other functions behave as before
+**Given** zero-valued input to the callers of the parser
+**When** `normalize("0m")`, `total([])`, `total(["0s"])`, `total(["0s", "1h"])` and `main(["0s"])` run (`main` checked via `capsys`)
+**Then** they return `"0s"`, `"0s"`, `"0s"`, `"1h"` and exit code 0 (printing `0`), as before
+
+## 🚫 Non-Goals
+- No new rejection in `normalize`, `total`, `format_duration` or the CLI.
+- No change to the grammar or to existing error messages for other invalid input.
+- No change to `format_duration(0) == "0s"`.
+
+## ⚠️ Constraints
+| Constraint | Value | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|
+| Test framework | `pytest` | already used in `tests/` |
+| Compatibility | public signature `parse_duration(text: str) -> int` unchanged | exported from `timeparse/__init__.py` |
+| Design implication | `schedule.py` and `cli.py` currently call `parse_duration`, so they must not inherit the new rejection | S3; the implementer chooses the mechanism (e.g. an internal non-rejecting helper) |
+
+## 🔒 Irreversible Decisions
+none
+
+## ✅ Verification Criteria
+| Scenario | Verification mode | Test name / manual step |
+|---|---|---|
+| S1 | unit | `test_zero_total_rejected` |
+| S2 | unit | `test_zero_unit_in_nonzero_accepted` |
+| S3 | unit | `test_other_functions_accept_zero` |
+
+### AC-001: zero total rejected
+Oracle: golden, the three inputs come verbatim from the requester's ask.
+
+### AC-002: zero unit in non-zero total accepted
+Oracle: golden, values come verbatim from the requester's ask (0h1m = 60 s, 1h0m = 3600 s by unit arithmetic).
+
+### AC-003: other functions unchanged
+Oracle: golden, expected values come from the existing `schedule.py` docstrings and current CLI behavior.
+
+## ❓ Open Questions
+none
+
+## 🔍 Refinement Decisions
+- Round 1 (light): ask is explicit; the only ambiguity was whether `normalize`/`total`/CLI should also reject zero. The third bullet answers it: they must not.
+- Lane `light`: one source file plus a helper, one session, `irreversible_decisions: []`.
+- No question tool was available, so the closing approval question was not asked.
+
+## 🔎 Spec Validation
+Advisory `spec-validator` pass (MAJOR_REVISION, non-gating):
+- Critical, declined: the `parse_duration` public contract change is not listed as irreversible. It is the requested feature, and a revert undoes it. There are no known external consumers in this repo. Kept `irreversible_decisions: []`; the DRI may overrule.
+- Critical, fixed: AC-003 lacked a `main(["0s"])` row; added.
+- Warning, fixed: AC-003 oracle evidence overclaimed docstring backing; corrected.
+- Suggestion, fixed: AC-001 widened to other all-zero spellings.
